MODIFICATIONS MADE BY THIS PROJECT
(stated in satisfaction of Apache-2.0 §4(b))

  - Default relay infrastructure removed. Upstream ships `RelayMode::Default`
    and `RelayMode::Staging`, which resolve to relay servers operated by
    N0, INC. Neither is reachable through this crate's public API. Relay
    selection is restricted to servers operated by the Rotelyx deployment.

  - Identity-publishing code deleted from the tree, not merely disabled. The
    `pkarr` and `dns` address-lookup providers and the `N0` / `N0DisableRelay`
    presets are gone. The generic DNS *resolver* is retained: it translates our
    own relay hostnames to addresses and has nothing to do with publishing
    identities.

  - Address lookup and discovery removed, not merely disabled. Upstream's
    default preset registers a pkarr publisher, a pkarr resolver, and a DNS
    address lookup against the `dns.iroh.link` zone operated by N0, INC.,
    which publishes the endpoint's public key to a third party at startup.
    Rotelyx performs rendezvous at the application layer instead.

  - Environment-based infrastructure override neutralised. Upstream honours
    the `IROH_FORCE_STAGING_RELAYS` environment variable to repoint relay
    infrastructure from outside the process. It has no effect here.

  - Path selection objective changed. Upstream selects network paths by
    latency. Rotelyx selects by metadata resistance, preferring a slower direct
    path over a faster relayed one.

  - Path-selection API exposed. Upstream keeps its `socket` module private,
    which makes the `PathSelector` trait impossible to implement from outside
    the crate even though the endpoint builder accepts one. A `path_selection`
    module re-exports the trait and its context types so that Rotelyx can supply
    its own selector.

  - Relay `ServerConfig` constructor added. The struct is `#[non_exhaustive]`
    and upstream ships no constructor, so the relay server cannot be started
    from another crate at all. Rotelyx operates its own relays, so a constructor
    was added; it leaves the metrics socket unset.

  - Default and staging relay modes deleted outright. Upstream's `RelayMode`
    carried `Default` and `Staging` variants resolving to relay servers operated
    by N0, INC., together with the `defaults::prod` and `defaults::staging`
    modules holding their hostnames and a `default_relay_mode()` function that
    selected between them from an environment variable. All of it is removed.
    `RelayMode` now has only `Disabled` and `Custom`.

  - Upstream examples and integration tests removed. They demonstrated the API
    that was deleted above and no longer compiled.

  - Public API renamed throughout to this project's own naming.

